  },
  {
    "field_name": "Main Goal",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Analyze GPU thermal and power behavior under combined CPU and GPU load"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Validation Objective",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Validates that stress-ng and the cuBLAS GEMM load (bin/gpu_stress) both run for the yaml duration and that peak GPU temperature, sustained (mean) GPU power, and uncorrectable GPU ECC errors are parsed from nvidia-smi samples taken every poll_interval seconds. The run fails if bin/gpu_stress does not start or report GEMMs, or if mean utilization.gpu is below half of gpu_load_percent (minimum 10%). Peak temperature above temp_threshold, mean power above power_threshold, or a hardware thermal slowdown event with throttle_check true marks every sample error"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Metrics",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "#1: Peak GPU temperature (peak_gpu_junction_temp_c); #2: Sustained GPU power (sustained_gpu_power_w); #3: GPU ECC error count (gpu_system_ecc_error_count); #4: Thermal throttle events (thermal_throttle_event_count)"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Command Tools Executed",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Run stress-ng --cpu --cpu-load, bin/gpu_stress (cuBLAS GEMM), and nvidia-smi --query-gpu"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Command Execution Details and Purpose",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Run bin/gpu_stress for yaml duration at gpu_load_percent (FP16 cuBLAS GEMM, busy for that percent of each 100 ms window) together with stress-ng --cpu --cpu-load --timeout, polling nvidia-smi temperature, power, utilization, thermal slowdown, and uncorrectable ECC each poll_interval, to measure combined CPU and GPU stress. DCGM and sensors are not run"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Command Methodology",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Start bin/gpu_stress at yaml gpu_load_percent, an FP16 cuBLAS GEMM that is busy for that percent of each 100 ms window, then run stress-ng --cpu --cpu-load for yaml duration. Poll nvidia-smi temperature, power, utilization, thermal slowdown, and uncorrectable ECC on poll_interval. DCGM and sensors are not run"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Execution Description With Parameters",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Runs stress-ng CPU workers and a cuBLAS GEMM GPU load (bin/gpu_stress) together while polling nvidia-smi every poll_interval seconds. num_threads: stress-ng --cpu workers (default 16). cpu_load_percent: stress-ng --cpu-load. gpu_load_percent: share of each 100 ms window the GPU runs FP16 GEMMs (default 50). duration: seconds (smoke 5, baseline 200, extended 580). temp_threshold and throttle_check: limits that mark samples error. power_threshold: maximum allowable GPU power draw in Watts (default 700 W). ecc_check: include the uncorrectable ECC count. output_format: csv"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Execution Domain",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Validation / Correctness"
  },
